  "text": "Thank you, all of you. You give me hope in digital spaces as a source of community.\n\nI used to be a 95% lurker, tentative dip-my-toe into comments and Notes type person.\n\nEvery article, every post I made washed me in anxiety. They were good opportunities for me to practice calming my body and push myself out of my comfort zone.\n\nFor the past six months, I’ve been regularly posting Notes, commenting on posts, and sending DMs.\n\nWhat I learned is — people are incredible, kind, generous, smart. You all make my brain light up every day.\n\nNow when I share a post, it feels like the start of a conversation, one of the good ones you know you’re going to want to settle into. Instead of picturing a giant no-shape monster waiting to gobble me up, my body is relaxed and excited to see what will come back.\n\n(Prior to six months ago, I never would have thought I could post about my daughter’s Rubik’s cube cake and have so much fun with it. 🤣)\n\nThat’s because of you and how you show up.\n\nThank you for sharing with us your fully human selves. I love our conversations, and especially about AI and not as AIs.\n\nSpecial shoutouts to @Natalie Nicholson @Dallas Payne @Kim Doyal @Mia Kiraki 🎭 @Elena | AI Product Leader @Karen Spinner @Karen Smiley @SheWritesAI @Dinah @Code Like A Girl @Rebecca Spitzer @Jason Ives @Caitlin McColl 🇨🇦 @JHong @Shannon Bindler @Jen Benford @AI Meets Girlboss @Monica Goh @Anna | how to boss ai. Getting to meet you and learn from you has been such a joy.\n\nYou all help me channel openness and creativity in the face of an uncertain future. Because you’re here, showing up, I’m excited about the future we can shape together.\n\n❤️❤️",
