  "text": "For my latest post, I had nearly 250% 2.5x the number of podcast downloads compared to total views.\n\nI started recording voiceovers as podcasts for my articles a couple months ago. I liked the idea of giving my audience another way to connect with me. \n\n(EDIT for details: This is the podcast article format, which is different from a regular article format. Regular articles do provide voiceover option, but the podcast format lets you use the recording like a true podcast with RSS feeds, episode info, show notes, and tracking # of downloads.)\n\nI was shocked to see that on average I get over 200% 2x the number of podcast downloads than views on the article. This is still true even for tutorial-like posts where I talk about how to build with AI, a format I wasn’t sure would work over audio only.\n\nIt’s humbling and exciting to picture hundreds of people listening to my voice as I share my learnings on how to use AI to expand what only you are able to do.\n\n(Thank you to @The Strategic Linguist for inspiring me to do voiceovers in the first place! When the queen of how language shapes perception tells you to share yourself through sound waves, you can’t really say no.)\n\nIf you are listener, thank you for letting my voice be part of your head space. Even if I can’t hear you in response, I feel the connection, and I appreciate it.",
